{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>first they shall set out.</b> Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: You find Judah first in every context — whether for encampment, for journey, for offerings, or for war. For encampment: ״the camps that encamp eastward — the standard of the camp of Judah״ (Numbers 2:3). For journey: ״the standard of the camp of Judah set out״ (Numbers 10:14). For offerings: ״he who offered on the first day was Nahshon son of Amminadav, for the tribe of Judah״ (Numbers 7:12). For war: ״Who shall go up for us against the Canaanite first? And HaShem said: Judah shall go up״ (Judges 1:1–2). And likewise for the future, when the bearer of tidings comes, Judah shall be informed first, as it says (Isaiah 52:7): ״How beautiful upon the mountains are the feet of the herald…״, and it is written (Nahum 2:1): ״Keep your festivals, O Judah…״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:40.862451318Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}